# Ownership for the CNAPP demo repository.
#
# QScanner reads this file (finding_owners, trace_finding, and the triage_to_owners prompt) to
# route a finding to the team that owns the file it lives in. Patterns are gitignore-style and
# the LAST matching rule wins, so the catch-all below only applies to paths no later rule
# claims.
#
# These team aliases are illustrative and do not exist in the nelssec org - the point of the
# demo is QScanner resolving a finding to an owner, not GitHub enforcing a review.

*                   @nelssec/platform-team

# Cloud infrastructure: Terraform, CloudFormation, Azure ARM
terraform/          @nelssec/cloud-security
cloudformation/     @nelssec/cloud-security
azure/              @nelssec/cloud-security

# Kubernetes packaging and the container build
helm/               @nelssec/platform-team
Dockerfile          @nelssec/platform-team

# Application code and its dependency manifests
app/                @nelssec/app-team
service/            @nelssec/app-team

# Pipelines, tooling, and docs
.github/            @nelssec/platform-team
scripts/            @nelssec/platform-team
docs/               @nelssec/app-team
